1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,750
Good morning.

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:07,740
Oh, good morning. Is this... er... room number 26?

3
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:08,770
Yes, that's right.

4
00:00:08,770 --> 00:00:11,800
So is this the Student Job Centre?

5
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:14,200
It certainly is. How can I help you?

6
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:19,160
Well, actually I'm looking for a job-a part-time job

7
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,900
Do you have anything available at the moment?

8
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:25,060
Ah, yes... Are you a registered student

9
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:28,680
I'm afraid this service is only available to full-time students.

10
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:33,830
Yes... I am. I'm doing a degree in Business Studies. Here's my student card.

11
00:00:33,830 --> 00:00:36,300
Which year are you in?

12
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:39,600
Well... I've been at university for four years

13
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:42,950
but I'm in the Third Year because I took last year off.

14
00:00:42,950 --> 00:00:48,529
Right... well, let's just have a look at what positions are available at the moment.

15
00:00:48,529 --> 00:00:52,993
There's a job working at the reception desk at the Sports Centre,

16
00:00:52,993 --> 00:00:56,340
for three evenings a week. That's Wednesdays, Thursdays and Fridays.

17
00:00:56,340 --> 00:01:01,300
That sounds like fun but unfortunately I have evening lectures

18
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:03,269
so that's not possible, I'm afraid.

19
00:01:03,269 --> 00:01:06,040
Is there anything during the day?

20
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:11,705
OK, that's no good then. Um. What about cleaning?

21
00:01:12,086 --> 00:01:15,200
There's a position for a cleaner at the Child Care Centre

22
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,310
Right...

23
00:01:16,310 --> 00:01:19,800
But you'd need to be there at 6 am. Does that appeal?

24
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:21,474
Six o'clock in the morning!

25
00:01:21,474 --> 00:01:24,840
Oh, that's far too early for me, I'm afraid

26
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:27,500
I'd never make it that early in the morning.

27
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:31,496
Mmm... Well. There was a position going in the Computer Lab.

28
00:01:31,496 --> 00:01:38,690
for three days a week that might be OK. Ah, here it is! No, it's in the Library,

29
00:01:38,690 --> 00:01:41,640
not the Lab., Clerical Assistant required

30
00:01:41,880 --> 00:01:45,484
I think it mostly involves putting the books back on the shelves.

31
00:01:45,484 --> 00:01:49,480
Oh no-hang on. It's for Wednesday and Friday evenings again.

32
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:52,050
NO. I can't manage that because of the lectures.

33
00:01:52,050 --> 00:01:54,268
OK, I'm getting the idea. Look,

34
00:01:54,268 --> 00:01:59,220
I'll just get a few details from you anyway

35
00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:02,400
and then we can check through the list and see what comes up.

36
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:09,150
We'll fill in the personal details on this application form first, if that's OK?

37
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:10,330
Yes, that's fine.

38
00:02:10,330 --> 00:02:12,000
Now, what's your name again?

39
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,940
Anita Newman. That's N-E-W-M-A-N.

40
00:02:16,940 --> 00:02:18,600
And your address, Anita?

41
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:23,740
I'm in one of the Halls of Residence for post-graduate students, you know, International House.

42
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:26,650
OK. That's easy. What's your room number there?

43
00:02:26,650 --> 00:02:33,200
Room B569 - no sorry B659. I always get that wrong

44
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:35,480
I haven't been living there very long.

45
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:38,850
Do you have any other skills? Typing, languages, that sort of thing?

46
00:02:38,850 --> 00:02:41,160
Well, I speak some Japanese.

47
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:43,983
Right, I'll make a note of that.

48
00:02:43,983 --> 00:02:46,403
Now-let's see what else is available.

49
00:02:46,403 --> 00:02:49,227
What do you think of administrative work?

50
00:02:49,227 --> 00:02:54,470
There is a position for an Office Assistant at the English Language Centre.

51
00:02:54,470 --> 00:02:56,420
That sounds interesting.

52
00:02:56,420 --> 00:03:01,600
It's for 3 days a week-Monday, Friday and Saturday mornings. Interested?

53
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:05,300
Mmm. I was hoping to have Saturdays free

54
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:11,110
But I need the work so... can you tell me what the job involves?

55
00:03:11,110 --> 00:03:16,600
Yes, sure. It says here that you'll be required to deal with student enquiries and answer the phone.

56
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:19,440
I'm sure I can handle all that without a problem.

57
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:23,440
Great. Well, would you like me to arrange an interview for you

58
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:25,250
Say, Friday morning, around ten?

59
00:03:25,250 --> 00:03:27,660
Could we make it a bit later

60
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:31,490
Unfortunately, I've got something to do at ten. Would that be OK?

61
00:03:31,490 --> 00:03:36,600
Not a problem. How about eleven thirty? Hope it works out for you Anita.

62
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:38,750
Me too. And thanks for all your help.
